          "rationale": "The authentic solution constructs P from the real and imaginary parts of conjugate(v)=(i,2-3i), giving columns (0,2) and (1,-3). Its determinant is -2, and these columns give AP=PC for C=[[1,-6],[6,1]], hence A=PCP^-1. This proves original option b (index 1), matching saved Correct grading. The stored Q=[[-1,0],[3,2]] is also valid: Q=PR with R=[[0,1],[-1,0]], and R commutes with C, so QCQ^-1=PCP^-1. Thus Q and P are unequal matrices that yield the same A; a normalizer must not equate their entries. This review documents the source-backed representative without declaring the alternative mathematically wrong."
